  You have permission to propagate covered works that you do not
convey, without conditions, so long as your license otherwise permits
propagation of covered works.  You may convey covered works to third
parties if you give them notice of this License, a copy of this
License, and information on how to obtain a copy of this License.  For
the avoidance of doubt, this exception does not apply to any derivative
work of a covered work, which is you create by modifying a covered work.

  If you distribute copies of the Library (or works based on the
Library) with contractual obligations regarding indemnification to the
recipients' of those copies against legal claims, for a reasonable fee or
for no charge; and you distribute the Library (or works based on the
Library) under the terms of this License, permitting propagation of
covered works under the conditions of this License; then you may not
distribute the Library or such works under other terms.  If you distribute
copies of the Library, you may use contractual protection to the extent
permitted by law, but any contractual protection you provide must be
consistent with this License and must not restrict the rights granted
by it.

  When you distribute covered works, you give recipients all the rights
that we gave you. Recipients of object code should have the legal right
to obtain the Corresponding Source for the work. The object code should
be prepared so as to require no more than ordinary effort to receive,
use, modify and propagate the Corresponding Source. The Corresponding
Source for a work in object code form means all the source code needed
to generate, install, and (for an object code work) run the object code
and to modify the work.

  5. Combined Works.

  You may convey a combined work under terms of your choice that,
taken together, effectively do not restrict modification of the
portions of the Library contained in the work and reverse engineering
for debugging such modifications, if you also do all of the following:

   a) Give prominent notice with each copy of the combined work that
   the Library is used in it and that the Library and its use are
   covered by this License.

   b) Provide a copy of this License.  If the combined work contains
   a notice that refers users to both this License and a document that
   covers a particular implementation of the Library, then the requirement
   in Subsection 4a to provide the copy of this License does not apply to
   you if you have already provided a copy of this License to the
   same recipient for the same work.

   c) For a combined work that displays copyright notices during
   execution, include the copyright notice for the Library among
   these notices, as well as a reference directing the user to the
   copies of this License and any associated documentation relating
   to the Library.

   d) Do one of the following:
       0) Convey the minimal corresponding source under the terms of
       this License, together with the copy of this License; or,
       1) under the same terms as this License (if that code is
       shared and the code and its documentation are made available to
       each other).

   e) Verify that user-already in possession of copies of this License
   and the combined work are permitted to continue to use their possessions
   covered by this License.

  If a facility in the combined work does not require an Application,
and is used with Equipment, then the Corresponding Source need not
include anything for Equipment.  This License applies to the Library or
works based on the Library.

